  Goal: [#D7D7AF][/dim]The sase TUI and waiting agent runners stop burning CPU and memory [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]on full-archive capacity scans: a warm capacity scan costs [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]milliseconds instead of 23 s, the TUI holds under 15% of one core [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]and a bounded heap on athena, and full GC collections respect a [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]duty-cycle bound.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim] Counts: [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]4[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] phases[dim][/dim] · [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]3[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] waves[/dim]\n[dim]   Path: [#87AFFF][/dim]plan:202611/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]capacity_scan_tui_runaway.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim] Prompt: [#87AFFF][/dim]prompts/202611/capacity_scan_tui_runaway.md[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Bead: [#87AFFF][/dim]sase-1sl[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Page: [#87AFFF][/dim]https://github.com/sase-org/sase--beads/blob/main/pages/sase-1sl/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]README.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim]  1 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]sase-core: capacity-only scan cost scales with live records, [/bold #D7AFFF] [bold white on #D75F87] large  [/bold white on #D75F87]\n      [bold #D7AFFF]not archive size[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]core-capacity-scan[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]core-capacity-scan: in the linked sase-core repo, add a statx-only [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]live-marker precheck plus meta-light closure classification (and, per [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]the verdict_cache decision, a sticky never-live verdict cache) to the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]capacity_only scanner path, with parity tests and a scan-cost bench [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]guarding identical retained records.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  2 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Ratchet the core pin and re-measure the scan on the real [/bold #D7AFFF]     [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n      [bold #D7AFFF]archive[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]sase-adopt-pin[dim] · [dim][/dim]after core-capacity-scan[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]sase-adopt-pin: move sase-core-revision.txt past the core commit, adopt [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]any new scan option in runner_slots/_scan.py, and re-measure cold/warm [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]capacity scans and runner-cache behavior on athena against the 22.9 s [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]baseline.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  3 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]TUI GC policy: full collections respect a duty-cycle bound[/bold #D7AFFF]    [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]gc-duty-cycle[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]gc-duty-cycle: record each full collection's duration in gc_policy.py [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]and defer the next full collection by last-pause times a duty factor [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF](clamped), applying the floor to idle and backstop triggers alike, with [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]fake-clock unit tests.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  4 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Measured verification on athena and residual-leak attribution[/bold #D7AFFF] [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]athena-soak[dim] · [dim][/dim]after sase-adopt-pin, gc-duty-cycle[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]athena-soak: soak a TUI instance on athena for at least an hour under [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]real agent load, verify CPU, rchar, RSS, GC-pause, and runner-CPU [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]targets against the 2026-11-12 baseline, and attribute any residual RSS [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]growth with the GC census.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]","clan_tribe":"epic","created_epic_ids":["sase-1sl.1.1"],"epic_bead_id":"sase-1sl","llm_provider":"codex","model":"gpt-6-astra","patch_name":"gh_sase-org__sase","phase_bead_id":"sase-1sl.1","reasoning_effort":"xhigh","role_suffix":"plan","vcs_provider":"GitHub","workf